IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- The Interpretation Act 1978 (1978 c. 30), the sections of construction and of powers: ss 3, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 14A, 18, 19,
-- 20(1), 20(2) and 21.
--
-- Source: the converter-made plain-text rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1978-30.txt, not the official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- A boolean named "section N provides that ..." answers FALSE when the section does NOT provide it. FALSE never means that the
-- opposite is the law: a contrary intention may displace the section, or the section may not reach the case.
-- Each section here opens with its own "unless the contrary intention appears" (or a variant), which every function takes as an
-- input; the caller decides whether one appears. Whether a section reaches a given enactment at all (Sch 2) is answered by
-- uk-interpretation-application.l4.
--
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (coverage table in NOTES.md): s 1 (a statement of drafting form that gives nothing to decide),
-- s 20(2A) to (6) and s 20A (EU material, and dates the text does not give), s 14A(6) (a definition of one word).

§ `Section 3: judicial notice`

-- src:10 | 3 Judicial notice.
-- src:11 | Every Act is a public Act to be judicially noticed as such, unless the contrary is expressly provided by the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 3 (src:10-11)
GIVEN `the contrary is expressly provided by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 provides that the Act is a public Act to be judicially noticed as such` `the contrary is expressly provided by the Act` MEANS
    NOT `the contrary is expressly provided by the Act`

§ `Section 6: gender and number`

DECLARE `Form of a word` IS ONE OF
    `a word importing the masculine gender`
    `a word importing the feminine gender`
    `a word in the singular`
    `a word in the plural`

-- Section 6 has three paragraphs and the Schedule 2 application differs for (a) and (c) against (b), so each is its own function.
-- A word includes itself without any section; the functions say FALSE for it, since section 6 does not provide it.

-- src:19 | 6 Gender and number.
-- src:20 | In any Act, unless the contrary intention appears,—
-- src:21 | (a) words importing the masculine gender include the feminine;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 6(a) (src:19-21)
GIVEN `the word asked about` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the word it is said to include` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 6(a) provides that a masculine word includes` `the word asked about` `the word it is said to include` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    AND `the word asked about` EQUALS `a word importing the masculine gender`
    AND `the word it is said to include` EQUALS `a word importing the feminine gender`

-- src:19 | 6 Gender and number.
-- src:20 | In any Act, unless the contrary intention appears,—
-- src:22 | (b) words importing the feminine gender include the masculine;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 6(b) (src:20) and (src:22)
GIVEN `the word asked about` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the word it is said to include` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 6(b) provides that a feminine word includes` `the word asked about` `the word it is said to include` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    AND `the word asked about` EQUALS `a word importing the feminine gender`
    AND `the word it is said to include` EQUALS `a word importing the masculine gender`

-- src:19 | 6 Gender and number.
-- src:20 | In any Act, unless the contrary intention appears,—
-- src:23 | (c) words in the singular include the plural and words in the plural include the singular.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 6(c) (src:20) and (src:23)
GIVEN `the word asked about` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the word it is said to include` IS A `Form of a word`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 6(c) provides that a word in one number includes` `the word asked about` `the word it is said to include` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    AND (   (`the word asked about` EQUALS `a word in the singular` AND `the word it is said to include` EQUALS `a word in the plural`)
         OR (`the word asked about` EQUALS `a word in the plural`   AND `the word it is said to include` EQUALS `a word in the singular`))

§ `Section 8: references to distance`

DECLARE `Way of measuring a distance` IS ONE OF
    `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`

-- A refusal is an expression at any type; each name is its message.
-- src:26 | 8 References to distance.
-- src:27 | In the measurement of any distance for the purposes of an Act, that distance shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 8 (src:26-27): "unless the contrary intention appears"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 8 gives no way of measuring a distance where a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 8 gives no way of measuring a distance where a contrary intention appears"

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 8 (src:26-27)
GIVEN `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Way of measuring a distance`
`section 8 — the way a distance is measured` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `the contrary intention appears`
    THEN `section 8 gives no way of measuring a distance where a contrary intention appears`
    ELSE `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`

§ `Section 10: references to the Sovereign`

DECLARE `Which Sovereign` IS ONE OF
    `the Sovereign for the time being`

-- src:30 | 10 References to the Sovereign.
-- src:31 | In any Act a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act is to be construed, unless the contrary intention appears, as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 10 (src:30-31): the section reaches a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act, and gives nothing where a contrary intention appears
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 10 gives no Sovereign unless the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act and no contrary intention appears` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 10 gives no Sovereign unless the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act and no contrary intention appears"

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 10 (src:30-31)
GIVEN `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which Sovereign`
`section 10 — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    THEN `the Sovereign for the time being`
    ELSE `section 10 gives no Sovereign unless the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act and no contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 11: construction of subordinate legislation`

-- src:32 | 11 Construction of subordinate legislation.
-- src:33 | Where an Act confers power to make subordinate legislation, expressions used in that legislation have, unless the contrary intention appears, the meaning which they bear in the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 11 (src:32-33)
GIVEN `an Act confers power to make subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11 provides that an expression used in the subordinate legislation has the meaning which it bears in the Act` `an Act confers power to make subordinate legislation` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `an Act confers power to make subordinate legislation`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 12: continuity of powers and duties`

-- src:35 | 12 Continuity of powers and duties.
-- src:36 | (1) Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty it is implied, unless the contrary intention appears, that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 12(1) (src:35-36)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 12(1) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

-- src:35 | 12 Continuity of powers and duties.
-- src:37 | (2) Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such, it is implied, unless the contrary intention appears, that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, by the holder for the time being of the office.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 12(2) (src:35) and (src:37)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 12(2) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, by the holder for the time being of the office` `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 14: implied power to amend`

DECLARE `Power to make an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a power to make rules, regulations or byelaws`
    `a power to make Orders in Council, orders or other subordinate legislation by statutory instrument`
    `a power to make some other instrument`

-- src:42 | 14 Implied power to amend.
-- src:43 | Where an Act confers power to make—
-- src:44 | (a) rules, regulations or byelaws; or
-- src:45 | (b) Orders in Council, orders or other subordinate legislation to be made by statutory instrument,
-- src:46 | it implies, unless the contrary intention appears, a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions or limitations, to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 14 (src:42-46)
GIVEN power IS A `Power to make an instrument`
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14 provides a power to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power` power `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `the contrary intention appears`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER power
         WHEN `a power to make rules, regulations or byelaws` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a power to make Orders in Council, orders or other subordinate legislation by statutory instrument` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a power to make some other instrument` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 14A: sunset and review provisions in subordinate legislation`

-- "Where a power is exercisable by the Scottish Ministers" or "within devolved competence" the section does not apply to that extent.
-- src:47 | 14A Power to include sunset and review provisions in subordinate legislation
-- src:48 | (1) This section applies where an Act confers a power or a duty on a person to make subordinate legislation except to the extent that—
-- src:49 | (a) the power or duty is exercisable by the Scottish Ministers, or
-- src:50 | (b) the power or duty is exercisable by any other person within devolved competence (within the meaning of the Scotland Act 1998).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 14A(1) (src:47-50)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power or a duty on a person to make subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or duty is exercisable by the Scottish Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or duty is exercisable by another person within devolved competence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14A applies to the power or duty` `an Act confers a power or a duty on a person to make subordinate legislation` `the power or duty is exercisable by the Scottish Ministers` `the power or duty is exercisable by another person within devolved competence` MEANS
        `an Act confers a power or a duty on a person to make subordinate legislation`
    AND NOT `the power or duty is exercisable by the Scottish Ministers`
    AND NOT `the power or duty is exercisable by another person within devolved competence`

DECLARE `Provision section 14A allows` IS ONE OF
    `a requirement to review the effectiveness of the legislation within a specified period or at the end of a specified period`
    `provision for the legislation to cease to have effect at the end of a specified day or a specified period`
    `provision of either of those kinds in relation to other subordinate legislation that the power or duty is being exercised to amend`
    `a requirement to consider whether the objectives remain appropriate and, if so, whether they could be achieved in another way`
    `provision generally or only in relation to specified provisions, cases or circumstances`
    `transitional, consequential, incidental or supplementary provision or savings in connection with such provision`

-- "The subordinate legislation may include": a permission. FALSE here means that section 14A does not give it.
-- (2)(c) needs the power to be exercised to amend other subordinate legislation; (3) is a kind of (2)(a); (4) and (5) attach to
-- subordinate legislation that includes provision of a kind mentioned in (2).
-- src:51 | (2) The subordinate legislation may include—
-- src:52 | (a) provision requiring the person to review the effectiveness of the legislation within a specified period or at the end of a specified period;
-- src:53 | (b) provision for the legislation to cease to have effect at the end of a specified day or a specified period;
-- src:54 | (c) if the power or duty is being exercised to amend other subordinate legislation, provision of the kind mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) in relation to that other legislation.
-- src:55 | (3) The provision that may be made by virtue of subsection (2)(a) includes provision requiring the person to consider whether the objectives which it was the purpose of the legislation to achieve remain appropriate and, if so, whether they could be achieved in another way.
-- src:56 | (4) Subordinate legislation including provision of a kind mentioned in subsection (2) may make such provision generally or only in relation to specified provisions of the legislation or specified cases or circumstances.
-- src:57 | (5) Subordinate legislation including provision of a kind mentioned in subsection (2) may make transitional, consequential, incidental or supplementary provision or savings in connection with such provision.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 14A(2) to (5) (src:51-57)
GIVEN `section 14A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Provision section 14A allows`
      `the power or duty is being exercised to amend other subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14A permits subordinate legislation to include` `section 14A applies` thing `the power or duty is being exercised to amend other subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF   NOT `section 14A applies`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `a requirement to review the effectiveness of the legislation within a specified period or at the end of a specified period` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `provision for the legislation to cease to have effect at the end of a specified day or a specified period` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `provision of either of those kinds in relation to other subordinate legislation that the power or duty is being exercised to amend` THEN `the power or duty is being exercised to amend other subordinate legislation`
        WHEN `a requirement to consider whether the objectives remain appropriate and, if so, whether they could be achieved in another way` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `provision generally or only in relation to specified provisions, cases or circumstances` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `transitional, consequential, incidental or supplementary provision or savings in connection with such provision` THEN TRUE

§ `Section 18: duplicated offences`

-- src:77 | 18 Duplicated offences.
-- src:78 | Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law, the offender shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law, but shall not be liable to be punished more than once for the same offence.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 18 (src:77-78): the liability to be prosecuted
GIVEN `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 18 provides that the offender is liable to be prosecuted under either or any of those Acts or at common law` `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 18 (src:77-78): "shall not be liable to be punished more than once for the same offence"
GIVEN `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 18 provides that the offender is not liable to be punished more than once for the same offence` `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `the act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 19: citation of other Acts`

DECLARE `Edition a citation is read as referring to` IS ONE OF
    `the revised edition of the statutes printed by authority`
    `the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission`
    `the Acts printed by the Queen's Printer, or under the superintendence or authority of Her Majesty's Stationery Office`

-- src:79 | 19 Citation of other Acts.
-- src:80 | (1) Where an Act cites another Act by year, statute, session or chapter, or a section or other portion of another Act by number or letter, the reference shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be read as referring—
-- src:81 | (a) in the case of Acts included in any revised edition of the statutes printed by authority, to that edition;
-- src:82 | (b) in the case of Acts not so included but included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission, to that edition;
-- src:83 | (c) in any other case, to the Acts printed by the Queen’s Printer, or under the superintendence or authority of Her Majesty’s Stationery Office.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 19(1) (src:79-83): the paragraphs apply to a citation of another Act, unless the contrary intention appears
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 19(1) gives no edition unless an Act cites another Act or a portion of one and no contrary intention appears` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 19(1) gives no edition unless an Act cites another Act or a portion of one and no contrary intention appears"

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 19(1)(a) to (c) (src:80-83)
GIVEN `an Act cites another Act by year, statute, session or chapter, or a section or other portion of another Act by number or letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cited Act is included in a revised edition of the statutes printed by authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cited Act is included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Edition a citation is read as referring to`
`section 19(1) — the edition a citation is read as referring to` `an Act cites another Act by year, statute, session or chapter, or a section or other portion of another Act by number or letter` `the contrary intention appears` `the cited Act is included in a revised edition of the statutes printed by authority` `the cited Act is included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT `an Act cites another Act by year, statute, session or chapter, or a section or other portion of another Act by number or letter`
             OR  `the contrary intention appears`
            THEN `section 19(1) gives no edition unless an Act cites another Act or a portion of one and no contrary intention appears`
        IF   `the cited Act is included in a revised edition of the statutes printed by authority`
            THEN `the revised edition of the statutes printed by authority`
        IF   `the cited Act is included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission`
            THEN `the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission`
        OTHERWISE `the Acts printed by the Queen's Printer, or under the superintendence or authority of Her Majesty's Stationery Office`

-- src:84 | (2) An Act may continue to be cited by the short title authorised by any enactment notwithstanding the repeal of that enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 19(2) (src:84)
GIVEN `the short title was authorised by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 19(2) provides that the Act may continue to be cited by the short title notwithstanding the repeal of the enactment` `the short title was authorised by an enactment` MEANS
    `the short title was authorised by an enactment`

§ `Section 20: references to other enactments`

-- "includes the words, sections or other parts referred to": a range is closed at both ends.
-- This is a rule about the parts of an enactment. It is NOT a rule about whether the first and last days of a period of time
-- are in the period (fork F1 in NOTES.md): the section speaks of "words, sections or other parts", and no day is one.
-- Positions are numbers, so the function reaches a part numbered 14A or 20A only through a position the caller assigns.
-- src:85 | 20 References to other enactments etc..
-- src:86 | (1) Where an Act describes or cites a portion of an enactment by referring to words, sections or other parts from or to which (or from and to which) the portion extends, the portion described or cited includes the words, sections or other parts referred to unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(1) (src:85-86)
GIVEN `the first part the Act refers to` IS A NUMBER
      `the last part the Act refers to` IS A NUMBER
      `the part asked about` IS A NUMBER
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(1) provides that the portion described or cited includes` `the first part the Act refers to` `the last part the Act refers to` `the part asked about` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    AND `the part asked about` AT LEAST `the first part the Act refers to`
    AND `the part asked about` AT MOST  `the last part the Act refers to`

-- "is a reference to that enactment as amended, and includes a reference thereto as extended or applied, by or under any other enactment".
-- src:85 | 20 References to other enactments etc..
-- src:87 | (2) Where an Act refers to an enactment, the reference, unless the contrary intention appears, is a reference to that enactment as amended, and includes a reference thereto as extended or applied, by or under any other enactment, including any other provision of that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 20(2) (src:85) and (src:87)
GIVEN `an Act refers to an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 20(2) provides that the reference is a reference to the enactment as amended, extended or applied` `an Act refers to an enactment` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
        `an Act refers to an enactment`
    AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`

§ `Section 21: interpretation`

-- src:99 | 21 Interpretation etc.
-- src:100 | (1) In this Act “Act” includes a local and personal or private Act; and “subordinate legislation” means Orders in Council, orders, rules, regulations, schemes, warrants, byelaws and other instruments made or to be made under any Act or made or to be made on or after IP completion day under any assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation as so defined or made or to be made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 21(1), "Act" (src:99-100)
GIVEN `the instrument is an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a local and personal or private Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 21(1) counts the instrument as an Act` `the instrument is an Act of Parliament` `the instrument is a local and personal or private Act` MEANS
        `the instrument is an Act of Parliament`
    OR  `the instrument is a local and personal or private Act`

-- "subordinate legislation" means ... instruments made or to be made under any Act, or made or to be made on or after IP completion day
-- under assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation, or on or after exit day under assimilated
-- direct CAP legislation. The dates of IP completion day and of exit day are defined in other Acts that are not among the sources,
-- so the caller says whether the instrument is made on or after them (fork F13).
-- src:100 | (1) In this Act “Act” includes a local and personal or private Act; and “subordinate legislation” means Orders in Council, orders, rules, regulations, schemes, warrants, byelaws and other instruments made or to be made under any Act or made or to be made on or after IP completion day under any assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation as so defined or made or to be made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation as defined in section 2 of the Direct Payments to Farmers (Legislative Continuity) Act 2020.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 21(1), "subordinate legislation" (src:100)
GIVEN `the instrument is made or to be made under any Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made or to be made on or after IP completion day under assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made or to be made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 21(1) counts the instrument as subordinate legislation` `the instrument is made or to be made under any Act` `the instrument is made or to be made on or after IP completion day under assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation` `the instrument is made or to be made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation` MEANS
        `the instrument is made or to be made under any Act`
    OR  `the instrument is made or to be made on or after IP completion day under assimilated direct legislation other than assimilated direct CAP legislation`
    OR  `the instrument is made or to be made on or after exit day under assimilated direct CAP legislation`

-- src:101 | (2) This Act binds the Crown.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 s 21(2) (src:101)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 21(2) provides that the Interpretation Act 1978 binds the Crown` MEANS TRUE
